course: dictionary
lesson: 6409
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word mushy can mean soft and squashy, or it can mean too sentimental. «The wood is chipped and cooked into a mushy pulp» is about texture, so mushy means soft and squashy here.
explain: The words around a word leave clues. «Anteaters get a specially made mushy mix that copies an ant diet» is about food, so the soft meaning fits. A film full of kissing and hugs can also be called mushy, but then the clues are about love and feelings, not about how something feels to touch.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «a soft and squashy mix» make sense? Yes. Does «a too sentimental mix» make sense? No, so the first meaning is right. Always try your meaning before you decide.
fact: Mushy means soft and squashy, like mashed food or over-ripe fruit.
fact: Informally, mushy also means too sentimental, full of soppy love feelings, as in a mushy film.
fact: «Mushy peas» are a British dish, often served with fish and chips.
fact: «Anteaters get a specially made mushy mix that copies an ant diet.»
fact: Useful phrases: «go mushy» means become soft, and «all mushy» means very soppy.
exercise: «The anteater's food is a mushy mix that copies an ant diet.» What does mushy mean here? | *Soft and squashy, like mashed food | Hard and crunchy like a biscuit | Cold and frozen | Full of soppy love feelings
exercise: Sam says, «That film was so mushy I was squirming!» What does mushy mean here? | Hard and shiny | Very quick and busy | *Too sentimental, full of soppy love feelings | Wet and muddy like a puddle
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you the mix is soft, not solid: «a mushy ant-like mix for the anteater». | *mushy | mix | ant | anteater
test: «Fruit that has gone mushy is soft and squashy, not firm.» What does mushy mean in this sentence? | Bright and shiny | Sweet and sticky | Too sentimental | *Soft and squashy
test: Mum says, «Don't go all mushy on me!» What does mushy mean here? | Covered in mud | Very hungry | *Soppy and too emotional | Soft and wet
exam: Why does the zoo give anteaters a mushy mix? | Because anteaters like soppy films | Because mushy food is always cheaper | *Because a zoo cannot collect enough wild ants | Because anteaters cannot chew at all
